{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_pq4meegafw4avx65fj6rj6zozt4hbljjr33ezm6x3igi6ioxtvoa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The whole C library is translated and verified.\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src/src/lib.c` (968 lines) is an inlined/expanded **`stb_ds.h`** implementation (Sean Barrett's dynamic array + hash map) plus two extra helpers (`strkey`, `sh_puts`). `c_src/include/lib.h` declares only `sh_puts`, but the `.c` file defines 16 non-static functions, all of which the CMake shared build exports. No namespace-renaming macros are involved — the `#define arrlen stbds_arrlen` family are macro→macro aliases only, so linker names equal source names.\n\n## Artifacts\n- `Cargo.toml` — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`\n- `src/lib.rs` — 1308 lines, 16 `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"` exports\n\n## Completion gate: symbol diff is empty\n`nm -D --defined-only` on both `.so` files → **16 vs 16, zero missing, zero extra**:\n`sh_puts, strkey, stbds_arrgrowf, stbds_arrfreef, stbds_rand_seed, stbds_hash_string, stbds_hash_bytes, stbds_hmfree_func, stbds_hmget_key, stbds_hmget_key_ts, stbds_hmput_default, stbds_hmput_key, stbds_hmdel_key, stbds_shmode_func, stbds_stralloc, stbds_strreset`\n\n## Byte-identical output verified\nTwo differential drivers (built once, linked against the C `.so` and the Rust `.so` via `$ORIGIN` rpath) exercise every export: array growth/free, sip-hash & string-hash over all tail lengths and byte-offsets, binary/big-key/string maps in all three key modes (`DEFAULT`/`STRDUP`/`ARENA`), tombstone reuse, table grow/shrink/rebuild, arena block escalation and oversized-string path, seed effects, and NULL/edge cases — dumping raw header and bucket internals (`hash[]`, `index[]`, seeds, thresholds). Result: **46,551 lines of output, `diff` empty, identical exit codes.**\n\n## C quirks deliberately preserved (not \"fixed\")\n- `hash ^= hash ^ ROTR(hash,n)` — the self-cancelling XOR that reduces to a plain rotate.\n- Sip-hash tail: `data |= (d[3] << 24)` is `int` arithmetic, so a high byte goes negative and **sign-extends into all upper 32 bits** of `size_t`, making lengths 4–7 hash identically. Confirmed against the C (`hi[4]==hi[5]==hi[6]==hi[7]`) and reproduced via `((x as u32) << 24) as i32 as usize`.\n- `sh_puts`'s `printf(\"%s %d\\n\", strmap[z], strmap[z].value)` passes a 16-byte struct through `...`; under SysV AMD64 it occupies two INTEGER eightbytes so `%s` eats `key` and `%d` eats `value`, with the third argument never read. Replicated as the ABI-equivalent two-argument call.\n- Unchecked `realloc` results, `static char buffer[256]` shared by `strkey`, and `assert()` semantics (routed to glibc `__assert_fail` with matching text/line/function).\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: my second test driver originally read `s[i].key` after `STRDUP`-mode deletions and segfaulted — **both** libraries crashed at the identical output line with the same exit code (139), which is a latent use-after-free in the original C, not a translation defect. I narrowed that loop to `value` only so the suite could run to completion."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1546,"cache_read_input_tokens":98822,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1546,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8223d0a0-9e2b-49a0-adbd-0f955151381c","uuid":"3a74fd3b-0e49-4c95-985c-382aa9a5f09b","timestamp":"2026-08-20T04:57:34.568Z"}
